    EXCERPT FIXTURE. The HEAD and DEFINEMEAS blocks and both MTSECT sections below
    are cut verbatim from a custodian file of the GSSA Copper Coast MT 2020
    open-file release (Geological Survey of South Australia, CC-BY-4.0, SARIG
    document record mesac2282), served in the AusMT corpus as
    surveys/copper-coast-2020/transfer_functions/edi/Wp01.edi.

    TWO EDITS, both stated so nothing here is taken for the custodian's file: this
    INFO block replaces the source's EPI-KIT JSON block, which records
    "EstimationsPerFrequency": 100; and every data block is truncated to its first
    seven frequencies, with NFREQ and the block comment counts restated to match.
    No value is altered.

    The source carries 101 sections: the averaged solution of record Wp01_avg,
    then XPR-0 to XPR-99, the per-frequency realisations that setting produced.
    The two kept here are the averaged solution and the first realisation. Both
    are fully populated and their ZXYR values differ at every frequency, so which
    section a reader returns is decided by the section NAMING RULE alone and not
    by which block happens to hold data.

    No angle bracket appears in this block on purpose: mt_metadata's DEFINEMEAS
    scanner keys on the two-character sequence anywhere in a line, INFO block
    included, and would read this prose as measurement metadata.

